Time Complexity: O(n)Auxiliary Space: O(1)2. Reverse TraversalReverse traversal is the process of visiting each element of an array starting from the last element and moving towards the first element. This method is useful when you need to process the elements of an array in reverse order. In this type of traversal, you begin from the last index (the rightmost element) and work your way to the first index (the leftmost element).
