Time Complexity: O(n)Auxiliary Space: O(1)Methods of Array Traversal1. Using For LoopA for loop is a control structure that allows you to iterate over an array by specifying an initial index, a condition, and an update to the index after each iteration. It is the most common and efficient way to traverse an array because the loop can be easily controlled by setting the range of the index. This method is ideal when you know the number of elements in the array beforehand or when you need to access each element by its index.
