Time Complexity: O(n)Auxiliary Space: O(1)2. Using While LoopA while loop is another method to traverse an array, where the loop continues to execute as long as the specified condition is true. The key difference with the for loop is that the loop control is more manual, and the counter or index is updated inside the loop body rather than automatically. The while loop can be useful when the number of iterations isn't predetermined or when the loop may need to stop based on a condition other than the array size.
            C++

    #include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
    int i = 0;

    cout << "Traversal using while loop: ";
    while(i < n) {
        cout << arr[i] << " ";
        i++;
    }
    cout << endl;

    return 0;
}


